    intro: "Forgiveness is wonderful, but the gospel offers even more. A pardoned prisoner is free but may be alone. God does more than pardon us; he adopts us. John says, 'See what kind of love the Father has given to us, that we should be called children of God; and so we are.' Salvation brings us into a family, with a Father who loves us, a Saviour who is our elder brother and a church full of brothers and sisters.",
    context: "In Roman society, adoption was a serious legal act that gave an adopted child all the rights of a natural-born child, including inheritance. Paul uses this to explain what Christ has done. In Galatians 4, he says that God sent his Son to redeem those under the law, so that we might receive adoption as sons. Ephesians 2 tells Gentile believers that they are no longer strangers and aliens but fellow citizens with the saints and members of the household of God, built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets.",
