    apply: "Set a simple plan for growth: choose a time each day for Scripture and prayer, join a small group or Bible study, and find one person who can encourage you. Review your progress at the end of the month. Thank God for any growth you notice.",
    activity: "Draw a plant on the board and label the roots, stem, leaves and fruit. Ask learners to match them with things in the Christian life: word and prayer (roots and water), fellowship (soil), trials (weather), fruit (character). Discuss what is needed for healthy growth.",
    takeHome: "Read 2 Peter 1:3-11, 2 Peter 3:14-18, Ephesians 4:1-16 and Philippians 2:12-18. Write a growth plan with three habits. Pray for patience with your own growth and others'.",
    prayer: "Ask God to help us to grow in grace and knowledge. Thank him for the means of grace. Pray for our church to be a place of growth.",
    teacher: "Some learners feel stuck or discouraged about their growth. Encourage them to look back at how far they have come and to focus on faithful habits rather than dramatic changes. Be careful not to compare learners with one another. Pair newer believers with more mature ones.",
    assess: "Weekly check: ask learners to name two means of grace and say how they help believers grow.",
    mcq1: ["What does 2 Peter 3:18 command?", ["Grow in the grace and knowledge of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ", "Seek wealth", "Avoid trials", "Rest from effort"], 0, "Peter commands growth in grace and knowledge."],
    mcq2: ["According to Philippians 2:13, who works in us?", ["God", "The church", "Our teachers", "Angels"], 0, "It is God who works in you."],
    tf: ["Spiritual growth happens automatically without any effort.", false, "Paul says to work out our salvation as God works in us."],
    sa: ["How does God cause believers to grow, and what should we do?", ["word", "prayer", "church", "trials", "spirit", "obey"], "A good answer says God causes growth by the Spirit through his word, prayer, the church and trials, and we cooperate through regular habits and obedience."],
